# Target C: close two additional order-2 `(2,2,2,2)` support orbits in the `p=3,m=4` branch

Date: 2026-09-23

Status: exact finite closure of two more stabilizer-order-2 support-set `S_7` orbits in the eight-no-root `k=5,D=-1,d_root=1,p=3,m=4,(2,2,2,2)` branch. This does not close the full `(2,2,2,2)` profile, the full `p=3` branch, the `k=5` layer, Target C-II, or Erdos Problem #99.

## 1. Support shard

The two support representatives are

```text
C = {1234,1235,1246,1357},
D = {1234,1235,1246,1567}.
```

The exact four-support orbit enumeration has eight stabilizer-order-2 support classes. The earlier shard-A certificate closed two of them. The companion verifier for this note selects exactly `C,D` from the same eight-class list and checks that their setwise stabilizers have order two.

For `(2,2,2,2)`, each support set has `3^4=81` cycle choices. These two support orbits therefore contain

```text
2 * (7!/2) * 3^4 = 408240
```

labeled eight-cycle sets. Quotienting cycle choices by the support stabilizers gives 45 cycle-set orbits for `C` and 42 for `D`, hence 87 `S_7` cycle-set representatives in this shard.

## 2. Necessary survivor conditions

The existing `p=3,m=4` reduction forces exactly three singleton touched root blocks, all remaining touched root blocks complete, touched-complete root nullity one, singleton coefficient rank three, and generalized weights

```text
(d1,d2,d3) >= (2,4,5).
```

For `D=-1,d_root=1`, the rank-three singleton coefficient system on eight external cycles has a five-dimensional coefficient nullspace. A survivor therefore requires external relation-rank increment five over the touched complete-root relation span. Untouched complete blocks cannot increase this quotient increment.

## 3. Exact finite census

A standalone exact reconstruction of the repository K8 coordinate normal form was run separately on both support classes. The results were

```text
C:
  S7 cycle-set orbits              45
  admissible singleton triples   8370
  singleton-direction states   225990
  coefficient-rank-three       225990
  generalized-weight states     14736
  external increment census {0:14736}
  max relation-row norm^2          70

D:
  S7 cycle-set orbits              42
  admissible singleton triples   8736
  singleton-direction states   235872
  coefficient-rank-three       235872
  generalized-weight states     12342
  external increment census {0:12342}
  max relation-row norm^2          70
```

Thus the aggregate shard census is

```text
S7 cycle-set orbits               87
admissible singleton triples   17106
singleton-direction states    461862
coefficient-rank-three        461862
generalized-weight states      27078
external increment census {0:27078}
```

Every generalized-weight-admissible state has external relation-rank increment zero, not five. Therefore neither support orbit contains a survivor.

> **Theorem.** In the eight-no-root `k=5,D=-1,d_root=1,p=3,m=4,(2,2,2,2)` branch, no state exists whose support set is in the `S_7` orbit of `C` or `D` above.

## 4. Exactness and validation

The support/cycle orbit enumeration, coefficient-rank test, and generalized-weight test were executed with exact integer/rational arithmetic. Relation rows are integral and ranked modulo

```text
P = 2^127 - 1.
```

The maximum squared Euclidean relation-row norm encountered is 70, and

```text
P^2 > 70^15.
```

Together with the repository's Lucas-Lehmer verification of `P`, the existing Hadamard argument rules out modular rank loss in the relevant minors, so the recorded relation ranks are exact over `Q`.

The committed repository wrapper was syntax-checked before upload. It was not executed from a checked-out repository during this run. The executed computation was a standalone reconstruction of the same coordinate construction, orbit enumeration, singleton filters, relation-row construction, and exact-rank criterion. `C` and `D` were executed separately and produced the counts above.

## 5. Remaining target

Before this run the open `(2,2,2,2)` support layer consisted of

```text
2 stabilizer-order-1 classes,
6 stabilizer-order-2 classes.
```

This theorem removes two more order-two classes. The exact remaining `(2,2,2,2)` support bottleneck is therefore

```text
2 stabilizer-order-1 classes,
4 stabilizer-order-2 classes,
```

for six support-set orbits total.

The four remaining order-two representatives are

```text
{1234,1235,1246,3457},
{1234,1235,1246,3567},
{1234,1235,1267,1456},
{1234,1235,1267,1467}.
```

The `(3,2,2,1)` profile remains open on the 35 touched-nullity-four support classes. The other unresolved `k=5` arithmetic branches remain

```text
D=-2, (d_root,p)=(0,5),
D=-1, (d_root,p)=(0,6).
```

The next direct finite target is another bounded external-rank-increment shard among the four remaining order-two `(2,2,2,2)` support classes.
